arenas is a new permanent mode in apex  legends the mode pits two teams of three  against each other in an elimination  style race to win three rounds  but you'll have to win by a round lead  of two to secure the dub  or you'll find yourself in a sudden  death round with chaos everywhere you go  put your prayers to the rng gods away  because there's  no looting necessary here instead at the  start of each round you're given a  select amount of materials that can be  spent to buy weapons  healing and ability uses the amount of  materials you receive increases each  round and you can get even more by  securing kills  or accessing canisters around the map  one canister gives each person on your  team  200 materials which could be the  difference between having no nomag and a  white mag on your gun which  we all know makes a major difference one  person can pick up the materials for  your entire team  but unlike in br once the canister is  used it can be used by the opposing team  that round  each kill is worth 75 materials so  having those extra materials for future  rounds can be  huge for closing out those close battles  only abilities and unspent materials  carry over to the next round  ultimate abilities cannot be purchased  before round three and can only be  purchased every other round  after you first buy one there are some  amazing ultimate combos to try like  valkyries and revenants  so go ahead and coordinate with your  team on when you're buying and using  those ultimate abilities for maximum  effects  unlike similar team deathmatch games  like rainbow six siege  and valorant there is no additional  objective to pursue each round like  disarming a bomb or capturing a flag  you just have to be the last team  standing and though you can revive down  teammates there is no respawn like in  battle royale  with no option of coming back you'll  have to find strategic ways to approach  each fight we already mentioned the  materials around the map which are worth  prioritizing if you want to spin big on  a future loadout  but if you're the type of player who is  always mindful of the ring in br  then you're in luck we may be in a small  arena but we can't escape the ring  so the rng gods are still kind of in  effect because you have to hope that the  ring is going to close in your favor  the rain can appear in various locations  throughout the match typically changing  for each round  moving the point of interest to  different areas around the map so each  round will always feel  a little unique alright alright it  wasn't exactly the whole truth that  there's no  looting there are healing resources to  be found in loot bins around the map  plus a single care package will drop in  a random spot midway through each round  delivering weapons and additional ammo  you can get a mozambique or p2020 for  free 99  so if you want to cash out on grenades  or abilities and roll the dice on  getting a weapon and other resources via  the care package or lubins  then that's another strategy too arenas  launches with  five maps consisting of new additions  and isolated points of interest from the  three  br maps the two new additions are party  crashers and phase runner while the  familiar three pois are kings canyons  artillery  world edges thermal station and  olympus's  golden gardens i appreciate the way  party crashers introduces a new map  while giving us a sense of familiarity  with mirage's boat being the life of the  party  as always so now that you get the gist  here are some general tips to help you  hop into arenas assuming you've played  apex legends before  beware of the peak wars resources are  scarce and if you get cracked early  that's going to leave you at a huge  disadvantage for the rest of the round  this makes characters like rampart  particularly devastating in arenas  when you thirst an enemy they will drop  a few resources  it's not always optimal to finish off  the kill mid-fight  but if you're really running dry on  heals just keep that in mind  while you do have to buy your abilities  legends like crypto who can recall their  abilities will be able to use it again  on a single charge  if you're like me you've become a little  bit reliant on the compass in vr to  communicate with your team but currently  in arenas there is  no compass so be prepared to adjust your  callouts  and mash those pings and the last  and biggest tip of all have fun this is  a brand new mode that is definitely  gonna spice things up and a great time  for you guys to hop back into apex  legends  especially if you've been away for a  while and now that you know a bit more  of the details  i want to know what you guys think is  the craziest ultimate team combo that  we're gonna see  once arenas is finally here so go ahead  and let me know down below in the  comments and of course  leave a like and subscribe to gamespot  for all the latest and greatest in your  gaming news and  more i'll go ahead and see you guys next  time but  play apex and have a good one peace out  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

